Device: Synaptics "Prometheus" / "Metallica MIS Touch" (USB 06cb:009a; also 138a:0090/0097/009d)

== Route 1: python-validity (userspace daemon) ==

Driver (userspace daemon): uunicorn
  https://github.com/uunicorn/python-validity
  License: MIT

fprintd-compatible DBus shim: open-fprintd
  (install alongside python-validity)

Protocol reverse engineering: nmikhailov, uunicorn and contributors
  https://github.com/nmikhailov/Validity90

Not a libfprint driver - a userspace driver daemon that registers with
open-fprintd so standard fprintd clients and pam_fprintd work.

== Route 2: native libfprint-2-tod1 (TOD) driver ==

Driver: Corrado Proietti (corradoproietti)
  https://github.com/corradoproietti/t480s-fingerprint-driver-for-linux
  Native Rust libfprint-2-tod1 match-on-chip driver; publishes a .deb.
  License: MIT OR LGPL-2.1-or-later (declared in Cargo.toml; the repository
  carries no LICENSE file).

Arch fork (the branch this entry's Arch package builds): blackandcold
  https://github.com/blackandcold/t480s-fingerprint-driver-for-linux
  branch arch-adoption, commit 216361ebeccb3d427844a4f15be8d6f96eaaf1c3
  Carries the Arch build fixes, the pre-TLS clean-slate init and the
  firmware-extension uploader that this sensor needs.

Arch packaging and the fixes above: hustles
  (AUR: libfprint-2-tod1-synaptics009a)
  https://github.com/hustles/libfprint-2-tod1-synaptics009a
  License: MIT (packaging), MIT OR LGPL-2.1-or-later (driver)

TOD-enabled libfprint: AUR libfprint-tod-git
  https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/libfprint-tod-git

Sensor firmware: the QMatcher firmware extension (6_07f_lenovo_mis_qm.xpfwext)
comes from Lenovo's Windows driver package (nz3gf07w.exe) and is downloaded at
build time, not mirrored here. Capture/init blobs in the driver originate in
Synaptics' Windows driver, as distributed by python-validity.
